<title>BELGIUM: Farm Council delays Plant Variety Office nomination.</title>
<headline>Farm Council delays Plant Variety Office nomination.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Farm Council decided on Monday to delay until its next meeting in December the appointment of a vice president of the European Union Plant Variety Office, a statement said.</p>
<p>The Office, which is provisionally based in Brussels pending a decision by the General Affairs Council on a permanent headquarters, registers plant seeds and standards.</p>
</text>
